==German==

===Alternative forms===
* [[Scheisse]] {{qualifier|Deutschland|Lichtenstein}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|schīze|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*skītaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*skei-d-||to part}}. Indo-European cognates include Ancient Greek {{term|σχιστός|lang=grc}} and English {{term|shit|lang=en}}, German Low German {{term|Schiet|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|schijt|lang=nl}}, Frisian {{term|skyt|lang=fy}}, Swedish {{term|skit|lang=sv}} within Germanic. Low German cognates sometimes used in standard German are {{term|Schiet|lang=de}} and {{term|Schitte|lang=de}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃaɪ̯sə/|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||-}}

# {{context|vulgar|lang=de}} [[feces]], [[shit]]
#: ''Wo ich hintrete nur '''Scheiße'''!''
# {{context|vulgar|figuratively|lang=de}} something worthless, [[shit]]
#: ''Das ist doch alles '''Scheiße'''!''

